But we do need to prove  $|H_{p_k}(\le n)|/|S_{p_k}(\le n)| = o(1)$  more rigorously (for fixed  $p$ ). Let  $\Psi(x,y)$  denote the  $y$ -[smooth number counting function](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smooth_number#Distribution). Because  $\Psi(x,p_k)$  is the number of nonnegative integer solutions to  $a_1\log{p_1}+\cdots+a_k\log{p_k}\le \log{x}$ , simplex volume comparisons (both lower and upper lattice point bounds are easy to estimate) yield
